Let's make sure this is right - you're standing right next to where the
door is.  You press '#100s' (or however it works on your system - possibly
just try 'ssssssssssss'), and you find nothing.  You then kick and there 
really was a door next to you.  Hmmmm.

You should have a 1/7 chance (or better) of finding a door on any given 
search.  A quick look at the code doesn't show me any factors which 
could make it worse than 1/7 per turn.

Did you compile this yourself?  If so, you might want to try in wizard mode,
with a lawful character (eg: knight), weilding +5 Excalibur (which should 
make the searching chances 1/2 per turn).  If you didn't compile this 
yourself, you may want to ask whoever did on your system.

If it turns out that you can find things with Excalibur, or with a ring
of searching, then probably, the key you're using to search is actually
waiting (or something).  If you're not the game administrator, I don't
know how you'd fix this, but you could probably figure out the key.

You might try searching 100 times, and then hitting ctrl-R, to redraw the
screen (maybe you are finding the things, but the screen is just not 
getting refreshed to show it).  If this is the case, it may have to do 
with the terminal type you're using versus what it was compiled for.

Aside from a bug in the random number generator on your system (rnl),
I can't suggest anything else that might be wrong.  But do get this 
figured out before continuing with your Valkyrie, because I doubt 
you'll be able to finish without ever searching (maybe you could with
a few wands of secret door detection, if they work for you).

